   "text": {
    "L1": "Numbers can be sorted by pairing their things. A full set of pairs is even; one left over is odd.",
    "L2": "Here is a common mistake: 34 is not odd just because it contains the odd digit 3.",
    "L3": "Only the ones digit decides. Tens and hundreds make full pairs.",
    "L4": "Look at 247. Its ones digit is 7, and 7 makes three pairs with one left over.",
    "L5": "So 247 is odd. The same rule says numbers ending in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8 are even; 0 is even too.",
    "L6": "Now add two odd numbers, such as 3 and 5. Their two leftovers pair up, making 8, an even number.",
    "L7": "Even plus even is even, while odd plus even stays odd because one leftover remains.",
    "L8": "Your turn: tap the number that is even."
   },
